---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../config";

const email = siteConfig.contactEmail;
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" canonicalPath="/en/privacy/" title="Privacy policy" description="What data Moon Poro Bot processes, why, for how long and how to delete it.">
  <section class="doc">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Updated: {siteConfig.lastUpdatedEn}</p>
    <p>Public verification still uses a League of Legends profile-icon challenge. Riot Sign On access has been approved; the new sign-in flow is undergoing local testing and has not launched publicly.</p>

    <div class="summary">
      <h2>In short</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We never see your Riot password or Riot account email.</li>
        <li>We store your Discord ID, Riot ID, region and rank to assign roles.</li>
        <li>No ads, no analytics, no tracking. We don't sell data.</li>
        <li>You can remove your link yourself with <code>/usun_weryfikacje</code>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>The data controller is {siteConfig.operatorName}, {siteConfig.operatorLocation}. For anything about your data, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. Never send us passwords.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. What we process</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Discord:</strong> your user and server IDs and the roles the bot manages. The prepared RSO flow also stores the Discord username and server name in the session to show which account is being linked.</li>
        <li><strong>Riot account:</strong> PUUID (a permanent Riot account ID), Riot ID, region and Solo/Duo rank (division, LP, wins, losses, inactivity), verification date and method, and rank refresh scheduling and state. During icon verification we also read the profile icon, but do not store it in the active account link.</li>
        <li><strong>Verification sessions:</strong> the prepared update stores session state, time and any error code for both profile-icon verification and Riot Sign On. This allows role assignment and audit work to finish after an interrupted operation.</li>
        <li><strong>Riot sign-in after RSO launches:</strong> Riot will provide your PUUID, Riot ID and region, without your password or email. A short-lived access token will be used only in process memory and discarded after retrieving the data. We do not request offline access or store a refresh token.</li>
        <li><strong>Moderation:</strong> warnings (who they concern, who issued them, reason, level, dates), monthly moderator statistics, and messages in moderation channels about verifications and about people who left, were removed from or were banned from the server.</li>
        <li><strong>Alt account protection:</strong> if an administrator turns it on, the bot checks how old your Discord account is when you join and bans accounts that are too new.</li>
        <li><strong>Administrator lookups:</strong> when an administrator checks which accounts are linked, we log who looked up whom, when and why.</li>
        <li><strong>IP address:</strong> after the RSO sign-in page launches, it will be kept briefly in the server's memory to limit attempts. This mechanism does not write it to the database.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical logs</strong> needed to fix errors.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The data comes from you, from Discord and directly from Riot Games. Accounts can't be linked without the Discord and Riot IDs.</p>
      <p>You can see your account and rank from the last refresh with <code>/profil</code>. Roles are visible to others on the server; moderation messages only to people with access to those channels.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Why and on what basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Verification, roles and <code>/profil</code></strong>: the service you ask for (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Moderation and server safety</strong>: preventing impersonation and alt accounts, overseeing administrator actions, fixing errors. This is our legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Legal obligations</strong>, e.g. answering a binding request from an authority (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The bot updates roles automatically but makes no decisions with legal effects.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Who has access</h2>
      <p>The operator and the server's administrators and moderators, as far as needed for moderation and support. Our service providers also process data: Discord, Riot Games and Google Cloud (the servers running the bot and database). They may do so outside the European Economic Area under the safeguards described in their own policies.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. How long</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account link and rank:</strong> until you or an administrator remove it. Leaving the server doesn't remove it, and the bot restores your roles if you come back.</li>
        <li><strong>Sessions in the prepared update:</strong> an icon challenge normally lasts 2 minutes and an RSO link 10 minutes. Completed or expired sessions of both methods are deleted after 7 days during the next daily cleanup. Work needed to finish assigning roles or handling audit messages is kept until completed.</li>
        <li><strong>Administrator lookup log:</strong> 90 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Warnings, statistics and moderation messages:</strong> as long as needed to moderate the server.</li>
        <li><strong>Database backups:</strong> up to 90 days. Deleted data may remain in a backup until then; backups are used only for disaster recovery.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical logs:</strong> size-limited, older entries are deleted.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Cookies</h2>
      <p>The static pages do not set cookies. After its public launch, the dynamic RSO service will set two strictly necessary cookies: <code>moon_poro_rso</code> to show the session result and <code>moon_poro_rso_browser</code> to confirm that sign-in finishes in the browser where it started. Both use HttpOnly, Secure and SameSite=Lax and expire 10 minutes after being set or renewed.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask for access to your data, correction, deletion, restriction or a copy, and you can object to processing. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We may ask you to confirm through Discord that the account is yours.</p>
      <p>You can also complain to the Polish data protection authority (Prezes UODO) or your local one.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change anything, we'll publish the new version here with a new date.</p>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
